file.content:
/* SignInDoor.tsx and CodeField.tsx: the Home page and the Agent page both
   load this, so it uses only the variables both define. Buttons are each
   page's own; this places them. The caller's column spaces the lines. */

.sign-in-title,
.sign-in-detail,
.sign-in-note,
.sign-in-error,
.sign-in-or {
  margin: 0;
}

.sign-in-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font: var(--font-section);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

.sign-in-detail,
.sign-in-note {
  font: var(--font-body-small);
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.sign-in-error {
  font: var(--font-label);
  color: var(--status-danger);
}

/* The design system's Button/Link: text only, Label Bold, action/primary. */
.sign-in-link {
  align-self: flex-start;
  padding: 4px 0;
  font: var(--font-label-bold);
  color: var(--action-primary);
  text-align: left;
  background: none;
  border: 0;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.sign-in-link:hover:not(:disabled) {
  color: var(--action-primary-hover);
  text-decoration: underline;
}

.sign-in-link:disabled {
  color: var(--action-disabled-text);
  cursor: default;
}

/* A link inside a sentence: the sentence's own type, in the link colour. */
.sign-in-link.inline {
  display: inline;
  padding: 0;
  font: inherit;
}

.sign-in-google {
  align-self: stretch;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: var(--button-primary-height);
  margin-top: 8px;
  font: var(--font-body-small-bold);
  background: var(--surface-raised);
}

.sign-in-google img {
  width: var(--sign-in-glyph-size);
  height: var(--sign-in-glyph-size);
}

/* "or" between two rules. */
.sign-in-or {
  display: flex;
  align-self: stretch;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  font: var(--font-body-small);
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.sign-in-or::before,
.sign-in-or::after {
  content: '';
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
}

.sign-in-email-row {
  display: flex;
  align-self: stretch;
  gap: 12px;
  margin: 0;
}

.sign-in-field {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  height: var(--button-primary-height);
  padding: 0 var(--sign-in-field-padding-x);
  font: var(--font-body);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  background: var(--surface-raised);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  border-radius: var(--sign-in-field-radius);
}

.sign-in-field:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--border-focus);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.sign-in-email-row button {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  justify-content: center;
}

/* The choice before anything is sent: the code button spans the column. */
.sign-in-code-button {
  align-self: stretch;
  justify-content: center;
  margin-top: 8px;
}

.sign-in-link-row {
  display: flex;
  align-self: stretch;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 12px;
}

.sign-in-links {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
}

.sign-in-link-dot {
  padding: 0 4px;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.sign-in-spinner {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: var(--sign-in-spinner-size);
  height: var(--sign-in-spinner-size);
  background: currentColor;
  -webkit-mask: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/refresh-cw.svg') center / contain no-repeat;
  mask: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/refresh-cw.svg') center / contain no-repeat;
  animation: sign-in-spin var(--sign-in-spin-duration) linear infinite;
}

@keyframes sign-in-spin {
  to {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
}

/* The design system's Field/Verification Code: six cells, one input. */
.code-field {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
  margin: 8px 0 4px;
}

.code-field input {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0;
  color: transparent;
  caret-color: transparent;
  background: transparent;
  border: 0;
  outline: none;
  opacity: 0;
}

.code-cell {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: var(--sign-in-code-cell);
  height: var(--sign-in-code-cell);
  font: var(--font-section);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  background: var(--surface-raised);
  border-radius: var(--radius-small);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle);
}

.code-cell.active {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--action-primary);
}

.code-field.refused .code-cell {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--status-danger);
}

tools.description:
Open the Browser pane: pass `url` to open a browser tab at a URL (no dev server needed — use this for external sites, staging, docs, or your deployed app), OR pass `name` to start a dev server from .claude/launch.json.

Start a dev server by name from .claude/launch.json. If .claude/launch.json doesn't exist, create it first with this format:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "<unique-name>",
      "runtimeExecutable": "<command>",
      "runtimeArgs": ["<args>"],
      "port": <port>
    }
  ]
}
Set "runtimeExecutable" to the command (e.g. "npm"), "runtimeArgs" to the arguments (e.g. ["run", "dev"]), and "port" to the server port. An optional "url" (http/https) opens the preview there instead of http://localhost:<port>. A localhost "url" must be just the server's origin — no path or query, matching the entry's port — for example "https://localhost:8443" or "http://app.localhost:3000"; to show a specific page, navigate after the preview opens. Non-localhost URLs may carry paths and are subject to the user's permission and the organization's browsing policy. A configuration with "url" and no command attaches to an already-running server. Only include servers you actually need to preview. Reuses the server if already running. ALWAYS use this instead of Bash for running servers. If the deliverable is already published as an Artifact, update the Artifact instead of starting a server to show it.

