9	
10	He said it right after the in-app sign-in change ([[sign-in-is-the-in-app-form-everywhere]]). That time the code (shared SignInDoor, the Preferences bridge messages, tests) was written first, and the canvas boards were redrawn only afterwards, in versions 140 and 141.
11	
12	**Why:** the canvas is the design source of truth ([[design-source-is-claude-artifacts]]). When the code comes first, the boards end up copying whatever the code happened to do. Kenneth then has no chance to change the design before code exists.
13	
14	**How to apply:** once a UI change is decided, edit the boards on the current canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ) first, publish them, and tell Kenneth which boards changed and what they show. Start the code only after that. If the code turns up something the boards didn't foresee, update the boards before writing the code that follows from it. Small fixes that change nothing on screen don't need a board.
